Here’s a **short, saveable cheat-sheet** you can copy into a note or README.
It’s minimal and tailored exactly to your `da4ml + conda + meson-python` setup.

---

# da4ml Editable Install (Meson / Conda) – Quick Guide

### Environment

* Conda env: `hgq2`
* Python: 3.12
* Source dir: `/mnt/ccnas2/bdp/bm920/da4ml`
* Build dir: `/mnt/ccnas2/bdp/bm920/da4ml/build/cp312`

---

## One-time setup (per env & Python version)

```bash
conda activate hgq2

# Clean old installs if needed
pip uninstall -y da4ml
rm -rf $CONDA_PREFIX/lib/python3.12/site-packages/*da4ml*

# Editable install from repo root
cd /mnt/ccnas2/bdp/bm920/da4ml
pip install -e .

# Initialize Meson build (THIS IS THE KEY STEP)
rm -rf build/cp312
meson setup build/cp312 . -Dbuildtype=release -Db_ndebug=if-release
ninja -C build/cp312
```

---

## Normal daily use (no rebuild needed)

```bash
python -c "import da4ml; print(da4ml.__file__)"
```

If it imports cleanly → you’re done.

---

## Rebuild only when needed

### If you change C++ / native code

```bash
ninja -C build/cp312
```

### If Meson config changes or build breaks

```bash
meson setup build/cp312 . --wipe
ninja -C build/cp312
```

---

## Common failure & fix

### ❌ Error on import:

```
ImportError: re-building the da4ml meson-python editable wheel package failed
```

### ✅ Fix:

```bash
ls build/cp312/build.ninja || (
  meson setup build/cp312 . -Dbuildtype=release -Db_ndebug=if-release &&
  ninja -C build/cp312
)
```

---

## Useful alias (optional)

```bash
alias da4ml-rebuild="ninja -C /mnt/ccnas2/bdp/bm920/da4ml/build/cp312"
```

---

## Mental model (1 line)

> **Editable Meson package = Python import hook + pre-existing Meson build dir**

No build dir → import fails. Build once → works forever (per env).

